# Generated code IS committed. No CI job runs `make proto`, `make sqlc` or
# `make tokens` -- CI goes straight to `make verify` -- so the tree has to
# compile exactly as checked out. That covers:
#   services/api/internal/db     (sqlc)
#   services/api/internal/gen    (buf -> Go)
#   packages/api-clients/gen     (buf -> TypeScript)
#   apps/manager/lib/core/api/gen(buf -> Dart)
# Never hand-edit any of it -- .claude/hooks/pre-edit-guard.sh blocks the
# paths it knows about, and regeneration would discard the edit regardless.
#
# EXCEPTION, and it is a live problem: *.g.dart below is still ignored, so
# `make tokens` output never lands in git. apps/manager/lib/app.dart imports
# core/theme/tokens.g.dart, which therefore does not exist in a fresh clone
# and the app cannot compile. Epic 08 has to resolve this -- either commit
# tokens.g.dart or make the Flutter CI job run `make tokens` first.

